  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nThe area remains in a Slight Risk for strong to severe\nthunderstorms into the evening. Currently a broken line of\nstorms is moving into eastern OH and NE KY and approaching WV.\nWith limited instability and outflows outpacing the deeper\nconvection, the threat appears limited. This is in line with\ncurrent CAMs showing a gradual weakening trend for convection \nas it moves into central and north/central WV. \n\nFurther south across the Coalfields, NE KY, and SW VA, there is\na little better instability and CAM support of another round of\nshowers/storms late afternoon into the evening. However the \nthreat looks to remain isolated and primarily be a damaging \nwind threat. Nonetheless, it will be closely monitored the rest \nof the afternoon. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nMuch colder air filters in behind the cold front tonight, with a\nfew snow flakes or wintry mix likely in the mtns. Even a dusting\nof snow will be possible across the highest peaks by early\nSunday morning. \n\nWhile temperatures will dip below 36 for some locales, \nclouds/wind should negate any frost development. A better \nchance is for the mtns and some foothill locations Sunday night \ninto Monday morning, where a Freeze Watch was issued. There \ncould be an expansion of frost/freeze headlines, especially for \nportions of SE OH, but confidence is too low at this time. There\ncould also be more snow showers for the mtns Sunday night into\nMonday, with light accumulations on the higher peaks.  \n\nAnother round of frost/freeze, which will be more widespread is\nexpected Monday night into Tuesday. This will likely impact \nlowland locations with an increasing likelihood of headlines. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...\n\nDaily min RHs will be in the 20s/30s percent range Sunday\nthrough Tuesday. A few disturbances will swing by the area, \nhopefully providing some relief to suppress fire danger in \ncertain areas, however these disturbances look very minor and \nmuch of the area will likely not receive any rainfall. With a \ngood wetting expected today into Sunday hopefully that will \nrefrain the fire danger threat for at least into Monday. \nRegardless, this setup will have to be closely monitored on a \ndaily basis and collaborated with local partners to see if any \nspecial weather statements will be needed.",
